<%-
  user       = ood_user
  tunnel_cmd = "ssh -N -L #{port}:127.0.0.1:#{port} -J #{user}@#{login_host} #{user}@#{host}"
  # Land on the viewer, not the control dashboard: the viewer is what this app is
  # for. `/viewer` is the SPA's declared route (no trailing slash), and the token
  # goes in the query string — the app moves it to sessionStorage and strips it.
  app_url    = "http://localhost:#{port}/viewer?token=#{biopb_token}"
  uid        = "biopb-#{port}"
-%>

<div class="well well-sm" style="margin-bottom:10px">
  <p style="margin:0">
    The BioPB web UI runs on <strong>127.0.0.1</strong> on the compute node and is
    not published to the network — it speaks plain HTTP, so exposing it would put
    your access token on the wire in the clear. Reach it through an SSH tunnel:
  </p>
</div>

<div style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <label style="display:block;margin-bottom:4px">
    <span class="label label-primary">Step 1</span>
    Run this on <em>your own computer</em> and leave it running:
  </label>
  <div class="input-group">
    <input type="text" readonly class="form-control" id="<%= uid %>-cmd"
           style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px"
           value="<%= tunnel_cmd %>">
    <span class="input-group-btn">
      <button class="btn btn-default" type="button"
              onclick="biopbCopy('<%= uid %>-cmd', this)">
        <i class="fa fa-clipboard"></i> Copy
      </button>
    </span>
  </div>
  <p class="help-block" style="margin-top:4px">
    It prints nothing and does not return — that is normal. Keep the terminal
    open for as long as you are using the browser. On Windows, run it in
    PowerShell or Windows Terminal.
  </p>
</div>

<div style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <label style="display:block;margin-bottom:4px">
    <span class="label label-primary">Step 2</span>
    Then open the browser UI:
  </label>
  <a href="<%= app_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
     class="btn btn-primary">
    <i class="fa fa-microscope"></i> Open BioPB Image Browser
  </a>
  <button class="btn btn-default" type="button"
          onclick="biopbCopy('<%= uid %>-url', this)">
    <i class="fa fa-clipboard"></i> Copy link
  </button>
  <input type="hidden" id="<%= uid %>-url" value="<%= app_url %>">
  <p class="help-block" style="margin-top:6px">
    The link carries your access token; the app stores it and strips it from the
    address bar. Open it rather than typing the address by hand — without the
    token you land on the unlock page. If you get <em>connection refused</em>,
    the tunnel in step 1 is not running.
  </p>
  <p class="help-block" style="margin-top:6px">
    <strong>The viewer says "Connecting to server…" until the catalog is
    built.</strong> That is the data plane indexing your directory, not a broken
    connection — a few hundred sources takes several minutes on a small core
    count, and there is no progress bar. The control dashboard, at
    <code>http://localhost:<%= port %>/</code>, works immediately and shows the
    server's state while you wait.
  </p>
</div>

<table class="table table-condensed" style="margin-bottom:0">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:11em;border-top:none">Data directory</th>
      <td style="border-top:none"><code><%= data_dir %></code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Compute node</th>
      <td><code><%= host %></code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Arrow Flight</th>
      <td>
        <code>grpc://127.0.0.1:<%= grpc_port %></code>
        <span class="help-block" style="display:inline;margin-left:6px">
          for the Python/Java SDK or napari, over the same tunnel
          (add <code>-L <%= grpc_port %>:127.0.0.1:<%= grpc_port %></code>)
        </span>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<script>
  function biopbCopy(id, btn) {
    var el = document.getElementById(id);
    var done = function () {
      var old = btn.innerHTML;
      btn.innerHTML = '<i class="fa fa-check"></i> Copied';
      setTimeout(function () { btn.innerHTML = old; }, 1500);
    };
    if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(el.value).then(done);
    } else {
      // Fallback for a non-HTTPS portal, where the async clipboard API is absent.
      var tmp = document.createElement("textarea");
      tmp.value = el.value;
      tmp.style.position = "fixed";
      tmp.style.opacity = "0";
      document.body.appendChild(tmp);
      tmp.select();
      try { document.execCommand("copy"); done(); } catch (e) { /* leave as-is */ }
      document.body.removeChild(tmp);
    }
  }
</script>
